    "https://nsuok.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/5938?c=nsuok": {
      "title": "FP9879 Part Time Faculty",
      "description": "FP9879 Part Time Faculty | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) FP9879 Part Time Faculty Broken Arrow, OK, United States | req5938 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/21/2026 Back to Search Adjunct Instructor for Health & Kinesiology (Broken Arrow) Department: Health and\nKinesiology. Courses to\nbe Taught: H ED 1113 – Principles of Health and Fitness/Wellness. H ED 2213 –\nFirst Aid/Responding to Emergencies. Position Overview: The Department of Health and Kinesiology\nis seeking an Adjunct Instructor to teach undergraduate-level courses in the\nareas of Health and Wellness and First Aid/Responding to Emergencies. The successful candidate will be expected to facilitate\nstudent learning across a variety of instructional formats including online,\nin-person, and hands-on environments. Qualifications: Demonstrated subject expertise in the areas listed above\nDocumented experience in online teaching environments. Commitment to high-quality instruction and student\nengagement Master’s degree or higher in a relevant field (Doctorate preferred). Job Duties: Deliver instruction in online, hybrid, or in-person formats. Engage students in interactive and applied learning. Evaluate student performance and provide timely feedback. Collaborate with department faculty to maintain\ninstructional quality and consistency. Uphold academic integrity and inclusive classroom practices. Anticipated Start Date: 1/11/2027 Compensation:\n$800 per credit hour. Apply Now Share Save Job Northeastern State University complies with all “applicable” federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination."
