    "https://nsuok.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/5931?c=nsuok": {
      "title": "N96612 Optician",
      "description": "N96612 Optician | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) N96612 Optician Tahlequah, OK, United States | req5931 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/15/2026 Back to Search Optician JOB\nSUMMARY This\nposition manages the operation of an assigned dispensary by providing patient\nservices, fabricating eyewear, dispensing eyewear, managing frame inventory,\nand assisting in the training of optometry students. MAJOR DUTIES Provides patient services; assists in the selection of frames and lenses; explains upgrade choices. Instructs optometry students in patient care, frame styling, and lens choices; reviews policies and procedures with new students and incoming residents; trains students in spectacle fabrication methods. Prepares or assists students in preparing work orders; enters prescription, size, material, and color information; reviews completed prescriptions; ensures compliance with specifications; notifies patients when glasses are ready; assists patients with glasses fitting; adjusts frame by hand or with appropriate tools; instructs patients in eyeglass care; prepares glasses for mailing to patients as requested. Traces and edges frames; edges and fits lenses for eyeglasses; repairs eyeglasses; tints lenses; marks progressive lenses; verifies lens powers. Maintains and calibrates equipment. Maintains supply inventory, including frame inventory; reorders as needed. Provides information to patients concerning insurance policies and procedures; processes insurance claims and determines patient deductible. Works with Cherokee National opticians with issues related to frames, lenses, insurance, or warranties. Cleans and tidies dispensary facilities; cleans mirrors, shelves and displays. Participates in industry continuing education opportunities. Performs related duties as assigned. KNOWLEDGE REQUIRED BY THE POSITION Knowledge of the standards, techniques, tools and equipment used in the fabrication of prescription eyewear. Knowledge of patient service principles and practices. Knowledge of eyeglass fitting and repair methods. Skill in the operation of computers and job related software programs. Skill in decision making and problem solving. Skill in interpersonal relations and in dealing with the public. Skill in oral and written communication. SUPERVISORY\nCONTROLS The supervisor assigns work in terms of general\ninstructions. The supervisor spot-checks completed work for compliance with\nprocedures, accuracy, and the nature and propriety of the final results. GUIDELINES Guidelines include Health Insurance Portability and\nAccountability Act requirements, patient care policies and procedures,\nprescription eyewear fabrication standards, insurance company policies, and\ncollege policies and procedures. These guidelines are generally clear and\nspecific, but may require some interpretation in application. COMPLEXITY/SCOPE OF WORK The work consists of related patient services and technical duties. Frequent interruptions contribute to the complexity of the position. The purpose of this position is to assist patients and fabricate and dispense eyewear. Success in this position contributes to the successful provision of services to dispensary patients. CONTACTS Contacts are typically with co-workers, physicians, patients, vendors, insurance representatives, and members of the general public. Contacts are typically to give or exchange information, to resolve problems, or to provide services. PHYSICAL DEMANDS/ WORK ENVIRONMENT The work is typically performed while sitting at a desk or table or while intermittently sitting, standing, stooping, walking, bending, or crouching. The employee frequently lifts light and heavy objects, climbs ladders, uses tools or equipment requiring a high degree of dexterity, and distinguishes between shades of color. The work is typically performed in an office or stockroom. The employee is exposed to noise and machinery with moving parts. SUPERVISORY AND MANAGEMENT\nRESPONSIBILITY None. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Knowledge and level of competency commonly associated with completion of specialized training in the field of work, in addition to basic skills typically associated with a high school education. Sufficient experience to understand the basic principles relevant to the major duties of the position, usually associated with the completion of an apprenticeship/internship or having had a similar position for one to two years. Possession of or ability to readily obtain a valid driver’s license issued by the State of Oklahoma for the type of vehicle or equipment operated. Annual salary $31,116.00 with excellent benefits, including generous leave time. Anticipated hire date: 11/09/2026 Applications will be accepted until: 10/18/2026 NOTE: Posting will close to applicants at 11:59 p.m., CST, on the date above. An application cannot be changed after it has been submitted. To complete the application process, it is critical to create a profile. NOTICE TO APPLICANTS It is Northeastern State University’s policy that all newly hired employees must provide an original social security card during the hiring process.  Failure to provide an original social security card will delay the hiring process and ability to begin employment. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Apply Now Share Save Job Northeastern State University complies with all “applicable” federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination."
    },
    "https://nsuok.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/5916?c=nsuok": {
      "title": "F99459 Assistant Professor in Psychology & Counseling",
      "description": "F99459 Assistant Professor in Psychology & Counseling | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) F99459 Assistant Professor in Psychology & Counseling Tahlequah, OK, United States | req5916 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/28/2026 Back to Search Assistant Professor of Counseling – Tahlequah Campus Job Description: The Department of Psychology and Counseling at Northeastern State University invites applications for a full-time faculty position in the M.S. in Counseling program. The M.S. in Counseling program is a CACREP accredited program with emphasis areas in Clinical Mental Health Counseling, Addiction Counseling, and School Counseling. The successful candidate will have the ability to teach in a variety of counseling courses, but particularly those pertaining to addictions counseling. A PhD in Counselor Education and Supervision is required. Dual licensure as an LADC and an LPC is preferred. NSU offers courses on all three campuses including Tahlequah, Broken Arrow, and Muskogee. The position is based on the Tahlequah campus. Responsibilities The successful candidate will be expected to teach addictions counseling courses and core counseling courses (both didactic and clinical, including supervision of practica/internship). All course delivery integrates technology. NSU seeks candidates with experience or who are willing to teach in blended and online formats when needed. Additional opportunities to teach summer classes for additional pay are available. Candidates are expected to maintain active membership and involvement with an appropriate professional organization (i.e. ACA, ACES, etc.). In addition to teaching, the position will involve student advisement, university service, and professional/scholarly contributions typically expected of a faculty member. The institution may revise the terms of this role based on changes in state laws or policies. Annual salary $57,610.00 with excellent benefits, including generous leave time. Anticipated hire date:  January 2027 Applications will be accepted until: 10/11/2026 (Applications will be reviewed as they are received NOTE: Posting will close to applicants at 11:59 p.m., CST, on the date above. An application cannot be changed after it has been submitted. To complete the application process, it is critical to create a profile. Notice to applicants It is Northeastern State University’s policy that all newly hired employees must provide an original social security card during the hiring process.  Failure to provide an original social security card will delay the hiring process and ability to begin employment. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Apply Now Share Save Job Northeastern State University complies with all “applicable” federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination."
    },
    "https://nsuok.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/5915?c=nsuok": {
      "title": "F99741 Assistant Professor of Health and Human Performance/Athletic Training, Tahlequah",
      "description": "F99741 Assistant Professor of Health and Human Performance/Athletic Training, Tahlequah | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) F99741 Assistant Professor of Health and Human Performance/Athletic Training, Tahlequah Tahlequah, OK, United States | req5915 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/28/2026 Back to Search Assistant Professor of Health and Human Performance/Athletic Training, Tahlequah Description of Position The Department of Health and Kinesiology at Northeastern State University is seeking an Assistant Professor of Health and Human Performance/Athletic training. Responsibilities 1. Twelve hours\nteaching load of undergraduate and graduate courses within the Department of\nHealth and Kinesiology. 2. Participate\nin college and department recruitment and retention efforts. 3. Participate\nin curriculum development and accreditation processes (CAATE). 4. Advise\nstudents within the department and 5. Maintain\nscheduled office hours. 6. Engage in\nscholarly activities internally or externally. 7. Collaborate\neffectively with department and college members. 8. Provide\nservice to the department, the College, and the University. 9. Collaborate with\nthe MAT Program Director on all recruitment and retention\nefforts specific to the MAT program. 10. Support the\nMAT Program Director and Director of Clinical Education in curricular\nplanning, compliance with CAATE standards and Higher Learning Commission\nrequirements. Qualifications 1. A doctoral degree in Kinesiology/Athletic Training or a related field is required.  Applicants who are in the process of completing their terminal degree and/or who are ABD will be considered. 2. BOC certification in good standing and eligible for Oklahoma State Licensure. 3. Two years of clinical athletic training practice/experience are preferred. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities 1. Evidence of\neffective teaching and scholarly work in exercise science/athletic training. 2. Capacity to\nteach across program levels (bachelor’s and master’s) 3. Ability to\nteach via instructional delivery methods including face-to-face, service-learning,\nand online. 4. Previous\ncollege/university teaching experience in an Athletic Training program. 5. Experience\nwith CAATE accreditation and clinical education coordination. Special Instructions to Applicants During the application process, the applicant will be required to upload a cover letter, a current curriculum vita, a statement of teaching philosophy, unofficial transcripts and contact information for three professional references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. An official/certified transcript is required upon employment. Please address all questions to the department chair (Dr. MooSong Kim) at kimm@nsuok.edu or 918-444-3217. Annual salary $56,130.00 with excellent benefits Projected hire date: 01/11/2027 Applications accepted until: 11/08/2026 NOTE: Posting will close to applicants at 11:59 p.m. on the date above. An application cannot be changed after it has been submitted. Notice to applicants It is Northeastern State University’s policy that all newly hired employees must provide an original social security card during the hiring process.  Failure to provide an original social security card will delay the hiring process and ability to begin employment. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Apply Now Share Save Job Northeastern State University complies with all “applicable” federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination."
    },
    "https://nsuok.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/5914?c=nsuok": {
      "title": "X96558 Assistant Director Communications, Tahlequah",
      "description": "X96558 Assistant Director Communications, Tahlequah | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) X96558 Assistant Director Communications, Tahlequah Tahlequah, OK, United States | req5914 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/27/2026 Back to Search Assistant Director Communications, Tahlequah JOB SUMMARY This position is responsible for preparing and maintaining statistical data and maintaining all communication platforms for undergraduate admissions and recruitment. Compile and analyze data to support recruitment initiatives; support the Director of Admissions & Recruitment. MAJOR DUTIES Assists in the development of the university’s recruitment targets, markets and goals. Serves as the undergraduate administrator for Radius. Manage recruitment communication to support recruitment and enrollment initiatives for prospective students. Contribute to the development and quality assurance of enrollment funnel reporting, integrate results into predictive modeling and performance reporting. Evaluates functionality of Radius, including operational and technical troubleshooting. Serves as the undergraduate administrator for Slate. Manage and coordinate outreach to support recruitment and enrollment initiatives for current and prospective students. Manage Call Center. Plan and coordinate social media presence for undergraduate admissions and recruitment. Assists with training and onboarding of new admissions and recruitment staff. Supervises daily operations within the Communications area. Assists with planning, organizing, and supervising annual recruitment events. Gathers and maintains current knowledge of university programs and services. Assists in enrollment management efforts as needed. Serves on assigned committees. Performs related duties as assigned. KNOWLEDGE REQUIRED BY THE POSITION Knowledge of higher education recruitment best practices. Knowledge of university admission processes, degree options, and housing procedures. Knowledge of university programs and services. Skill in the operation of computers and job related software programs. Skill in decision making and problem solving. Skill in interpersonal relations and in dealing with the public. Skill in oral and written communication. COMPLEXITY/SCOPE OF WORK The work consists of maintenance and development of all communication platforms for student recruitment and enrollment management reporting duties. The high volume of student contacts contributes to the complexity of the position. The purpose of this position is to recruit students for NSU through various communication strategies. Success in this position contributes to the successful recruitment of students. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree from an accredited university. Experience sufficient to thoroughly understand the work of subordinate positions to be able to answer questions and resolve problems, usually associated with two to three years experience or service in a university recruitment or admission office. Possession of or ability to readily obtain a valid driver’s license issued by the State of Oklahoma for the type of vehicle or equipment operated. Must be capable of maintaining regular attendance. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Master’s degree and previous experience with Slate CRM preferred. Annual salary $43,896.00 with excellent benefits, including generous leave time. Anticipated hire date: 11/9/2026 Applications will be accepted until filled NOTE: Posting will close to applicants at 11:59 p.m., CST, on the date above. An application cannot be changed after it has been submitted. To complete the application process, it is critical to create a profile. NOTICE TO APPLICANTS It is Northeastern State University’s policy that all newly hired employees must provide an original social security card during the hiring process.  Failure to provide an original social security card will delay the hiring process and ability to begin employment. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Apply Now Share Save Job Northeastern State University complies with all “applicable” federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination."
